# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "System sizes and computational requirements {#system-sizes-and-computational-requirements}"
msgstr "Laki ng sistema at mga kinakailangan sa computation {#system-sizes-and-computational-requirements}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The computational cost of SQD is dominated by the eigenstate solver calls. At each step of the self-consistent configuration recovery iteration, n\\_batches of eigenstate solver calls are performed. The different calls are embarrassingly parallel. In this [tutorial](/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization), those calls are inside a for loop. **It is highly recommended to perform these calls in parallel**.\n"
msgstr "Ang computational cost ng SQD ay pangunahing nagmumula sa mga tawag sa eigenstate solver. Sa bawat hakbang ng self-consistent configuration recovery iteration, may n\\_batches na tawag sa eigenstate solver. Ang mga tawag na ito ay embarrassingly parallel. Sa [tutorial](/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization) na ito, nasa loob ng for loop ang mga tawag na iyon. **Lubos na inirerekomendang patakbuhin ang mga tawag na ito nang parallel**.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.solve_fermion()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.solve_fermion \"qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.solve_fermion\") function is multithreaded and capable of handling systems with \\~25 spacial orbitals and \\~10 electrons with subspace dimensions of \\~\\$10^7\\$, using \\~10-30 cores.\n"
msgstr "Ang function na [`qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.solve_fermion()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.solve_fermion \"qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.solve_fermion\") ay multithreaded at kayang humawak ng mga sistemang may \\~25 spacial orbital at \\~10 electron na may subspace dimension na \\~\\$10^7\\$, gamit ang \\~10-30 core.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choosing subspace dimensions {#choosing-subspace-dimensions}"
msgstr "Pagpili ng mga subspace dimension {#choosing-subspace-dimensions}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The choice of the subspace dimension affects the accuracy and runtime of the eigenstate solver. The larger the subspace, the more accurate the calculation, at the cost of increasing the runtime and memory requirements. The optimal subspace size of a given system is not known; thus, a convergence study with the subspace dimension can be performed, as described in this [guide](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/choose-subspace-dimension).\n"
msgstr "Nakakaapekto ang pagpili ng subspace dimension sa accuracy at runtime ng eigenstate solver. Habang mas malaki ang subspace, mas tumpak ang kalkulasyon, pero tumataas ang runtime at memory na kailangan. Hindi alam ang pinakamainam na laki ng subspace para sa isang sistema; kaya puwedeng magsagawa ng convergence study gamit ang subspace dimension, gaya ng inilalarawan sa [gabay](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/choose-subspace-dimension) na ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bounding the subspace dimension {#bounding-the-subspace-dimension}"
msgstr "Paglilimita sa subspace dimension {#bounding-the-subspace-dimension}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `samples_per_batch` argument of [`qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian \"qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian\") sets the number of bitstrings contained in each batch, and thereby controls the subspace dimension indirectly: in the case of quantum chemistry applications, its value sets an upper bound to the subspace dimension. The dimension that actually results depends on how many of the sampled bitstrings are distinct, and it grows over the course of the self-consistent configuration recovery iterations, so it is not known in advance. See this [example](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/select-open-closed-shell) for more details.\n"
msgstr "Ang argument na `samples_per_batch` ng [`qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian \"qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian\") ang nagtatakda ng bilang ng mga bitstring sa bawat batch, kaya hindi direktang kinokontrol nito ang subspace dimension: sa mga aplikasyon sa quantum chemistry, ang value nito ang nagtatakda ng upper bound sa subspace dimension. Ang dimension na aktwal na lalabas ay nakadepende sa kung ilan sa mga na-sample na bitstring ang magkakaiba, at lumalaki ito habang umuusad ang mga self-consistent configuration recovery iteration, kaya hindi ito alam nang maaga. Tingnan ang [halimbawang ito](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/select-open-closed-shell) para sa mas maraming detalye.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `max_dim` argument of the same function bounds the dimension directly, by limiting the number of CI strings retained in each spin sector. Since the subspace is spanned by the Cartesian product of the two spin sectors, `max_dim=d` caps the subspace dimension at `d**2`, while a tuple `max_dim=(d_a, d_b)` limits the spin-alpha and spin-beta sectors separately, capping the subspace dimension at `d_a * d_b` (with `symmetrize_spin=True`, the two limits must be equal). When a batch yields more CI strings than the limit allows, the strings requested through `include_configurations` and those carried over from the previous iteration are retained preferentially, and the remaining slots are filled with the most frequently sampled strings. Because it caps the size of the largest diagonalization that the eigenstate solver will be asked to perform, `max_dim` is a convenient way to keep the solver within a runtime and memory budget. See this [guide](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/choose-subspace-dimension) for more details.\n"
msgstr "Direktang nililimitahan ng argument na `max_dim` ng parehong function ang dimension, sa pamamagitan ng paglilimita sa bilang ng mga CI string na itinatago sa bawat spin sector. Dahil ang subspace ay binubuo ng Cartesian product ng dalawang spin sector, ang `max_dim=d` ay naglilimita sa subspace dimension sa `d**2`, habang ang tuple na `max_dim=(d_a, d_b)` ay hiwalay na naglilimita sa spin-alpha at spin-beta sector, na naglilimita sa subspace dimension sa `d_a * d_b` (kapag `symmetrize_spin=True`, dapat magkapareho ang dalawang limit). Kapag mas maraming CI string ang nabuo ng isang batch kaysa sa pinapayagan ng limit, mas pinipiling panatilihin ang mga string na hiniling sa pamamagitan ng `include_configurations` at ang mga dinala mula sa nakaraang iteration, at pinupunan ang natitirang puwesto ng mga pinakamadalas na na-sample na string. Dahil nililimitahan nito ang laki ng pinakamalaking diagonalization na hihilingin sa eigenstate solver, ang `max_dim` ay isang maginhawang paraan para panatilihin ang solver sa loob ng budget ng runtime at memory. Tingnan ang [gabay](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/choose-subspace-dimension) na ito para sa mas maraming detalye.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Solvers {#solvers}"
msgstr "Mga solver {#solvers}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The projection and diagonalization steps are performed by a classical solver. We provide here two generic solvers, one for Fermionic systems and another for qubit systems. Other solvers that might be more efficient for specific systems can be interfaced by the users.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga hakbang ng projection at diagonalization ay isinasagawa ng isang classical solver. Nagbibigay kami rito ng dalawang generic na solver, isa para sa mga Fermionic na sistema at isa pa para sa mga qubit system. Maaaring i-interface ng mga user ang iba pang solver na posibleng mas episyente para sa mga partikular na sistema.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trim SQD {#trim-sqd}"
msgstr "Trim SQD {#trim-sqd}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Standard SQD diagonalizes each subsampled batch independently and keeps the best result, so the number of configurations it can consider is limited to what one affordable subspace can hold. **Trim SQD** instead partitions the bitstrings into batches, performs an intermediate diagonalization of each batch, then performs a larger diagonalization using the highest-weight determinants from each partition. This method is based on joint research from the Cleveland Clinic Foundation, RIKEN, and IBM [\\[7\\]](#references), and can be enabled by passing a [`TrimPolicy`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/trim#qiskit_addon_sqd.trim.TrimPolicy \"qiskit_addon_sqd.trim.TrimPolicy\") object to the [`diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian \"qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian\") function.\n"
msgstr "Ang karaniwang SQD ay dina-diagonalize ang bawat subsampled na batch nang hiwalay at itinatago ang pinakamahusay na resulta, kaya ang bilang ng mga configuration na maaari nitong isaalang-alang ay limitado sa kayang hawakan ng isang abot-kayang subspace. Sa halip, ang **Trim SQD** ay hinahati ang mga bitstring sa mga batch, nagsasagawa ng intermediate diagonalization sa bawat batch, at saka nagsasagawa ng mas malaking diagonalization gamit ang mga determinant na may pinakamataas na weight mula sa bawat partition. Ang paraang ito ay batay sa magkasanib na pananaliksik ng Cleveland Clinic Foundation, RIKEN, at IBM [\\[7\\]](#references), at maaaring i-enable sa pamamagitan ng pagpasa ng [`TrimPolicy`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/trim#qiskit_addon_sqd.trim.TrimPolicy \"qiskit_addon_sqd.trim.TrimPolicy\") object sa function na [`diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian \"qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian\").\n"

